'Reconstructs committed history and eligible participants','A2':'Restart restores persisted term/vote while resetting transient authority support'},unknowns=['Snapshot transport, file validation and on-disk initialization corner cases remain unmapped'])\nfacts=[dict(id='F-committed',meaning='This node records a committed log prefix through committed, under its local log and configuration history; application completion is separate.',identity={'cluster':'clusterID','prefix':'log indexes through committed'},validity_context='Local retained log/snapshot history, including current-term quorum advancement, leader-advertised bounded commit or snapshot evidence; not a client completion assertion.',representation=['entryLog.committed','pb.State.Commit','snapshot.Index'],durability='Persisted through engine SaveRaftState; raft transition itself is memory-only.',recovery='ReadRaftState and latest snapshot reconstruct prefix; constructor checks bounds.',source_ids=['src-core-commit-reset','src-core-term-election','src-log-commit','src-node-replay'],unknowns=['Storage crash behavior below LogDB has not been reviewed']),dict(id='F-read-pending',meaning='A leader queue record retains a read request original SystemCtx, requester and sampled committed index until prefix release or authority reset; confirmed holds distinct responding senders for that context, not an external completion.',identity={'cluster':'leader clusterID','request':'SystemCtx High/Low','requester':'readStatus.from'},validity_context='Transient leader readIndex instance; multi-voter request admitted after current-term commit; reset replaces instance. Prefix confirmation may increase recorded index before consumption.',representation=['readIndex.pending','readIndex.queue','readStatus.ctx/from/index/confirmed'],invalidators=['B-authority','B-read-confirm'],durability='Volatile only.',recovery='New readIndex on reset/restart; requester has separate timeout state.',source_ids=['src-read-prefix','src-read-confirm-send','src-core-commit-reset'],unknowns=['Whether remote prefix-release output preserves request identity','Whether membership changes invalidate retained confirmations'])]\nacts=[]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nfor a in roles:\n relevant=[b for b in bs if b['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary='; '.join(b['trigger'] for b in relevant),entry_points=[b['id'] for b in relevant],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for b in relevant for s in b['source_ids']))))\ncore=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation, authority, persistence, membership, recovery and consumption paths have been read. Local anomalies and deeper variants remain open; this is navigation, not coverage or correctness evidence.',formation=dict(explanation='Node batches proposals into Peer under raftMu. Leader stamps term/index, replicates to members and advances commitment from voting match order statistic only for its current term. Followers require preceding term match and protect the committed prefix, replying after engine persistence. Conflicts reduce next and retry; snapshots resynchronize missing history. Engine exposes committed entries to the RSM queue, whose application/session results and applied index drive client consumption. ReadIndex separately samples committed index, gathers heartbeat confirmation and releases pending prefixes to local readiness or remote responses.',behavior_ids=['B-replicate','B-read-admit','B-read-confirm','B-persist','B-apply','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-pending'],source_ids=['src-core-commit-reset','src-core-term-election','src-engine-order','src-rsm-apply','src-read-confirm-send']),context=dict(explanation='Per-cluster term, role and applied membership define authority. Timers launch elections for eligible full members only after committed work is applied; votes require fresh log and no conflicting vote. Candidate quorum promotes and appends a current-term no-op. Higher terms demote/reset; lower terms are rejected. CheckQuorum may revoke leadership; transfer waits for target match and uses TimeoutNow, while proposals are dropped during transfer. Configuration application changes participant maps and local removal revokes leadership. Restart restores persisted term/vote/log but initializes transient follower context.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-members','B-recovery','B-persist'],source_ids=['src-core-term-election','src-core-commit-reset','src-raft-candidate','src-raft-timers','src-node-members','src-raft-init']),connection=dict(explanation='Term dispatch precedes response consumption. Reset clears old votes, replication progress and pending ReadIndex support while retaining established log/commit; leader must form current-term commitment before multi-voter reads. Log freshness and committed-prefix protection constrain future leaders. Election waits for application so committed membership changes affect later quorums; RSM changes update Peer under raftMu. Old client work can be dropped or time out independently of preserved decisions. Read confirmation is transient; exact context and applied-index checks bridge its publication to requester completion, making remote prefix correlation a concrete unresolved consumption premise.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-members','B-replicate','B-read-admit','B-read-confirm','B-read-forward','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-pending'],source_ids=['src-core-term-election','src-core-commit-reset','src-node-members','src-read-prefix','src-read-confirm-send','src-read-consume']),open_details=['Remote prefix read-response correlation','Pending read confirmation eligibility across membership transitions','Concrete LogDB crash guarantees and snapshot transport','Transport batching and message-loss history for a fixed witness'],core_gaps=[])\nmapdata=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Dragonboat Go module: NodeHost APIs, per-cluster raft/Peer, engine scheduling, LogDB boundary, RSM and transport boundaries. Application state-machine behavior remains caller-owned; in-repository storage/transport internals are not externalized merely because injectable.',protocol_contexts=['ClusterID/NodeID, current term, role, applied membership, log index and read SystemCtx'],external_interfaces=['NodeHost proposal/ReadIndex APIs','IStateMachine/IOnDiskStateMachine','LogDB and message transport'],ownership=['Node raftMu serializes peer transitions; RSM application and pending-request owners synchronize separately'],source_ids=['src-api-contract','src-api-read','src-node-step','src-engine-order']),activities=acts,behaviors=bs,facts=facts,core_overview=core,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm'],reason='Remote response context differs from local prefix member context; preserve as Candidate premise.',source_ids=['src-read-confirm-send'],high_consequence=False),dict(entry_point='raft.handleLeaderHeartbeatResp / membership transitions',disposition='deferred',reason='Read-support producer/eligibility across changes needs composed history, not fabricated observer replies.',source_ids=['src-read-confirm-send','src-raft-members-change'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='LogDB SaveRaftState / snapshot transport',disposition='deferred',reason='Core call ordering read; backend atomicity and transferred-file validation not yet traced.',source_ids=['src-engine-order'],high_consequence=True)])\nopen('map.json','w').write(json.dumps(mapdata,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nq=dict(question='When one heartbeat context confirms a prefix containing earlier forwarded reads, does leader publication preserve each released request identity so its requester can consume the qualified result?',importance='A lost identity can strand an otherwise confirmed remote read until timeout; this is a completion/correlation concern, not presently a demonstrated linearizability violation.',source_ids=['src-read-prefix','src-read-confirm-send','src-read-follower','src-read-consume','src-node-read-batch','src-api-read','src-read-test'],participants=['Leader','Forwarding follower','Voting heartbeat responders'],objects=['readStatus','ReadIndexResp','requester pendingReadIndex batch'],contexts=['Stable multi-voter term after current-term commit','Two distinct SystemCtx values pending concurrently'],event_paths=['node.handleReadIndex -> Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forward -> leader addRequest -> later-context heartbeat confirm -> prefix release -> ReadIndexResp -> addReady'],activity_classes=['A1'],behavior_ids=['B-read-admit','B-read-confirm'],fact_ids=['F-read-pending'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-read-forward':'Actual exact-context consumer and independent batch creation','B-authority':'Term/reset validity of pending confirmation','B-persist':'Production response dispatch boundary'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Local prefix completion uses s.ctx correctly','Single-context remote confirmation retains the same context','Requester timeout/GC supplies bounded cleanup, so no permanent waiting claim is made','Periodic heartbeats reissue latest pending context, but released records are removed'],unknowns=['Construct a legal message history where later context gains quorum while an earlier remote context remains pending; inspect transport ordering before selecting delivery policy.','Ground local identity-preservation duty and distinguish it from any unsupported successful-completion deadline.'],trigger_rationale='The release loop addresses each original requester but encodes the confirming message context, despite an exact-context downstream lookup. Source work already rules out forced serialization of client batches; a short controlled history can distinguish the consequence.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\ns=dict(action='continue',map_path='map.json',sou